WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.869
GRADY POWELL: Well,
gentlemen, congratulations.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.236
The two of you guys
are moving forward

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:05.805
into round three
of the competition,

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.407
where we send you
to your home forges

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.974
to build one of
these two weapons

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.677
from our "Forged
in Fire" vault. And

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:18.651
the weapon you'll be building
in round 3 is the pira sword.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.519
DAVY WILSON: I'm
seeing this sword

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.490
with a wonky, Zorro-shaped
handle, and about a 24-

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.259
to 28-inch blade.

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.561
And I'm thinking, not so bad.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.163
I think I can make this.

00:00:30.263 --> 00:00:32.131
DOUG MARCAIDA (VOICEOVER):
Featured in season 7 of "Forged

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:35.368
in Fire," the pira is an
ornate, versatile sword

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.604
used by the Yakan tribe in
the southern Philippines.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.106
The weapon's unique blade
shape and long pommel

00:00:41.206 --> 00:00:43.142
proved to be challenging
for both smiths, who

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.077
were ultimately
forced to start over

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:46.979
the third day of their builds.

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.348
Ultimately, one smith
was unable to secure

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.084
the mechanical connection
to her handle in time,

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:54.987
forcing the judges to issue
a vote of no confidence,

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:56.322
due to safety concerns.

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:58.157
GRADY POWELL: You will have
four days at your own forges

00:00:58.223 --> 00:01:00.527
to work on your pira
blades, so good luck.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:01.394
We'll see you then.

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.567
GARRETT KEMBLE: My
name is Garrett Kemble.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:10.803 line:8%
I'm 41 years old, and
I've been bladesmithing

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:11.704 line:14%
for about two years.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.139
What I like about
bladesmithing is

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:15.241
it's a big, hot
piece of steel, you

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.043
can't take your eye
off that, and you

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.344
have to be in the moment.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.914
The first thing I'm going to
do is get the forge fired up.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.016
Now that I'm roughly
to shape, feels good,

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:25.985
I'm going to go over
to the belt grinder

00:01:26.051 --> 00:01:28.154
so I can cut more material away.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:31.457
I check parameters,
and I'm dead on.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.725
Murdered it.

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:34.193
We're pretty close to quenching.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.462
I'm ready to heat treat.

00:01:38.397 --> 00:01:40.433
We might have to quench again.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.168
She's not skating
like she should.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.337
I'm not happy with
the file test,

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:45.738
so I'm going to quench again.

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:48.441
I just don't think it
sat in there long enough.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.979
This quench, temperature
looked better,

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:55.915
looked more even,
a longer quench.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.083
All right, we're good.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:02:00.086
I start working on what's
essentially a guard.

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:03.789
I'm drilling it out to
make it fit the tang.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:04.924
It was a little fiddly.

00:02:05.024 --> 00:02:06.926
I'm hesitant about the
fit and the quality,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.129
but overall I'm happy.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.665
Side note, this is the only
piece of this wood I have.

00:02:15.101 --> 00:02:16.269
Everything's going smoothly.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.876 line:8%
DAVY WILSON: I'm Davy
Wilson, I'm 49 years old,

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:25.511 line:14%
and I'm a master barber.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:28.214 line:8%
Unfortunately, I'm losing
the master barber's

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.550 line:14%
hair on top of my head.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:33.085
My dad and I took
a class together,

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:35.421
and after we built
our very first knife,

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:38.224
I looked over and said, hey,
you want to build another one?

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:39.526
He said, I sure do.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:44.130 line:8%
Part of the reason I am here
now is to make Dad proud.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:44.964 line:14%
Hey, Dad.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:45.831 line:14%
 Hey.

00:02:45.898 --> 00:02:47.499
 Had a visitor this morning.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:49.736
Just about to get
started on this sword.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.771
Any time in the past
when Dad would stop in,

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.774
he'd jump right in and help
me with the knife build.

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:57.543
I don't know if he was
disappointed or relieved

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.712
that he didn't have to
help with this build.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.881
 I'd like to help on
something like that,

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:04.583
but least it's a shorter one.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:05.651
 That's right.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.720
It's different than
anything we've done before.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:08.655
 I'll see you later.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.489
 All right, see you.

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:11.657
Feels good.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:14.193
I believe that he's going
to be extremely proud of how

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:15.494
this blade performs.

00:03:15.594 --> 00:03:18.430
I believe we got a
good, straight blade.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:21.801
I'm having trouble just getting
this walnut cut through,

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.336
having to use some chisels.

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:25.672
Sometimes it needs
a little persuasion.

00:03:28.841 --> 00:03:32.578
Whoo, finally it works.

00:03:32.678 --> 00:03:35.682
Once we epoxy and pin
the blade to the handle,

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:38.517
it's going to be one
homogeneous piece.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:40.319
Looking good, it's
holding there.

00:03:40.385 --> 00:03:42.355
I've got the handle to
a comfortable point.

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:43.756
Now it's time to test.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:47.626
It's pretty sharp, but it's
not where it needs to be.

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.630
For my first pira, I'm
pretty happy with it.

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.699
DOUG MARCAIDA: Bladesmiths,
welcome to the KEAL test.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:55.334
To find out how lethal
your weapons are,

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:56.702
according to its
historic design,

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.204
I'm going to take your
weapon and deliver

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:01.507
some lethal blows on
whatever's behind the curtain.

00:04:01.573 --> 00:04:03.008
I'm going to find
out how effective

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.343
your weapons are,
at the same time

00:04:04.409 --> 00:04:06.445
how they feel when I wield them.

00:04:06.545 --> 00:04:08.013
Garrett, you're first.
You ready for this?

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:08.781
 Yup.

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.315
 Let's do this.

00:04:10.415 --> 00:04:11.717
GARRETT KEMBLE: I don't
know if they're just

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:13.686
going to swing through
the sheet at whatever's

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:14.954
on the other side.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:18.391
It's just, you know, one more
game in the forge of mystery.

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:24.897
[music playing]

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:40.746
 All right, Garrett, let's talk
about your pira sword, here.

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:44.150
Your handle
construction, well done.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.684
Your edge is very sharp.

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:49.555
It allows me to cut deeply and
swing well with your weapon.

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.790
Overall, sir, it will KEAL.

00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:52.625
 Thank you.

00:04:52.691 --> 00:04:54.126
 All right, Davy,
are you set, sir?

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:54.927
You're next.

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:55.762
 Yes, sir.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:02.435
[music playing]

00:05:14.446 --> 00:05:15.915
DOUG MARCAIDA: All
right, Davy, let's talk

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.516
about your pira sword, here.

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:21.120
First up in your design, it's
a very forward-heavy weapon.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:24.089
As you can see just by looking
at the spine, it's thick here,

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:26.992
and it tapers down to the guard.

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:29.061
Now, your edge is sharp.

00:05:29.128 --> 00:05:33.332
With the forward weight, it
chops into the pig carcass.

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.801
But slicing, not
quite because you

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.803
have to control the
weight of the weapon.

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:40.706
But it will KEAL.

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:41.474
 Yeah, it will.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:48.247
DAVE BAKER: Gentlemen,
you know what time it

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:51.550
is, the mystery strength test.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:53.019
Now, these strength
tests are not

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.620
concerned about
what your blades do

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.491
to the target, more what that
target does to your blades.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:59.659
Garrett, you're up first.

00:05:59.726 --> 00:06:00.292
Are you ready?

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:01.127
 Let's do it.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.939
GRADY POWELL: Damn,
the guard, the weld.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:14.440
 Right, yeah.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.674
 Right where he welded.

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:16.509
 Yeah.

00:06:32.791 --> 00:06:35.828
 So, Garrett, right off, I
liked the feel of the weapon.

00:06:35.894 --> 00:06:38.196
The balance was nice,
the weight was nice.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:39.599
I had no issues.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.602
Looking at that break, your
grain structure is beautiful.

00:06:42.702 --> 00:06:44.637
All I can really say
is that that tang

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:46.839
is a little on the lean side.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:48.707
And maybe that where
this married up,

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:51.343
there was just enough
movement in there

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.212
that it allowed
it to blow apart,

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:55.047
as opposed to being
tight and held together.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:55.948
 Mhm.

00:06:56.015 --> 00:06:58.183
 But it definitely
felt like a nice weapon.

00:06:58.283 --> 00:06:59.085
 Thank you.

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:06.392
 Garrett, that is painful
to see, man, but you

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:08.193
are not out of the fight yet.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:12.832
Davy, your blade has to survive
one strike on this brutal test.

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.666
And if you do, you win.

00:07:14.733 --> 00:07:17.369
Dave.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:21.040
[music playing]

00:07:33.652 --> 00:07:35.821
DAVE BAKER: All right, Davy,
man, there's a lot of weapon

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:36.455
here.

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:37.623
Your grinds are beautiful.

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:40.326
I think your handle's
beautiful and comfortable.

00:07:40.392 --> 00:07:42.294
There's no edge
damage on this at all.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.429
 Awesome.

00:07:43.495 --> 00:07:45.564
 I would not run my
finger down this blade.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.099
You nailed the
heat treat on that.

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:47.866
Good job.

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:48.701
 Thank you.

00:07:52.037 --> 00:07:54.273
GRADY POWELL: Well,
Davy, the bell is rung,

00:07:54.373 --> 00:07:56.909
and you survived it,
man, congratulations.

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.645
Garrett, we hate
to see this happen.

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.280
We always want to see
more testing done,

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:04.083
but unfortunately, your blade
did break during the testing.

00:08:04.149 --> 00:08:05.217
We can't continue.

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:07.720
For that reason, today you
are not the "Forged in Fire"

00:08:07.787 --> 00:08:08.887
champion.

00:08:08.954 --> 00:08:10.656
I want to say thank
you for coming out,

00:08:10.723 --> 00:08:13.025
and I have to ask you to
please leave the forge, man.

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:14.026
 Thanks.

00:08:14.093 --> 00:08:16.128
GRADY POWELL: Davy, your
blade survived the test,

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:18.764
and that makes you the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.467
You're going to be leaving here
with a check for $10,000, man,

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:22.267
congratulations.

00:08:22.334 --> 00:08:23.135
 Thank you.

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:24.803
[applause]

00:08:24.903 --> 00:08:26.305
 You have any
plans for the money?

00:08:26.371 --> 00:08:28.741
 A little more
mustache grooming stuff.

00:08:28.808 --> 00:08:29.642
[chuckles]

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:33.245
I am so elated right now.

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:34.313
Thank you so much.

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:36.382
Knowing where my
journey started, when

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:39.084
I didn't know anything
about swinging hammers

00:08:39.184 --> 00:08:40.552
and forging metal.

00:08:40.652 --> 00:08:44.256
Dad, I'm the new "Forged
in Fire" champion.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:46.926
I'm coming home a winner.

